## Text

Section text is [CommonMark](https://commonmark.org/help/) Markdown:
_italic_, **bold**, `code` and [links](https://go.dev/).

- bullet lists
- with several items
  continued on the next line

1. numbered lists
2. work too

// A line starting with // is a comment and is not shown.

: Lines starting with ": " are speaker notes for this slide.

## Code blocks and quotes

Indented or fenced blocks are shown as code, without running anything:

```
$ go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/present@latest
```

> Clear is better than clever.

\.play and the other commands start with a period; a backslash before it shows the line as text.

## Links and HTML

.link https://go.dev/ The **Go** website

.html html/badge.html

.iframe html/frame.html 120 600

: .link shows a single link on a line of its own; its label is inline Markdown.
: .html includes a file as raw HTML; .iframe embeds a page.

